    {
      "filename": "Photographers who never move (8291565472).jpg",
      "title": "File:Photographers who never move (8291565472).jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0b/Photographers_who_never_move_%288291565472%29.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Photographers_who_never_move_(8291565472).jpg",
      "width": 4928,
      "height": 3280,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Takashi Hososhima from Tokyo, Japan",
      "description": "This photo might have interesting light decoration, but I think there is more interesting thing on this photo. Look at the photographers front of the large fountain, and realize how clear their silhouette is! Guess what? This photo is actually taken in 10 seconds, which means the photographers never moves during I took this photo. They are so amazing, aren't they? I bet they took a great photos there :D\nこの写真はただのイルミネーションの写真ではなく、ほかに驚くべき事実が隠されています。大きな噴水の前で写真を撮っている人、シルエットがくっきりハッキリ移っていますね。実はこれ、10秒のシャッター速度で撮りました。つまり、あのカメラマンは10秒間全く微動だにしなかったいうことです。なんという集中力でしょうか！きっとあのカメラマンはとてつもなく美しい写真を撮ったに違いありません。\n\n[ Nikon D4, Nikon AF-S NIKKOR 70-200mm f/2.8G ED VR II, 200mm, f/8.0, 10sec, ISO100, Lightroom 4.2, Tripod ]",
